# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# .dockerignore — controls what gets sent to the docker daemon as
# build context for BOTH apps/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# The Hetzner host always builds from a clean ``git clone``, so the
# entries below mostly protect against:
#   1. Local-developer ``docker compose build`` runs accidentally
#      shipping 2-3 GB of venv / node_modules / .next into the image.
#   2. Re-runs on the host after the first deploy (when ``.next`` and
#      friends start to accumulate from rebuilds).
#   3. Defence-in-depth: never bake .env files into image layers, even
#      if a Dockerfile accidentally tried to ``COPY``.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/

# Node / Next.js — apps/web/Dockerfile does its own ``npm install`` in
# the deps stage; the host's node_modules must not pollute that.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.npm/
.yarn/

# Env files — never bake secrets into an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Supabase CLI runtime state
apps/web/supabase/.temp/
apps/web/supabase/.branches/

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs / runtime artifacts
*.log
**/*.log
model_cache/
.cache/

# Docker artifacts (when building from inside a CI runner)
Dockerfile.*~
docker-compose.override.yml
